course: dictionary
lesson: 4197
title: Goose and geese
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A goose is a big bird with a long neck and webbed feet. It often lives on farms or near water. «At the park pond Jake tries to feed the geese.» Here geese is the plural of goose: one goose, many geese. The spelling changes, so do not add an s.
explain: Context helps you when goose is used in a different way. In «Jake calls his brother a goose», the words around it show that goose is not about a bird. When someone is called a goose, they are being silly.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If you read «you goose» and swap in "bird", it does not make sense, so the meaning must be silly. Always ask whether your meaning still fits.
fact: A goose is a big bird with a long neck and webbed feet.
fact: A male goose is called a gander, and a baby goose is called a gosling.
fact: Geese is the plural of goose: one goose, many geese.
fact: «Goose bumps» are tiny bumps on your skin when you are cold or scared.
fact: In autumn, geese migrate in V-shapes, and «you goose» means you are being silly.
exercise: Which word is the plural of goose? | *geese | gosling | goose | gooses
exercise: What is a baby goose called? | goose | gander | *gosling | duckling
exercise: «Goose bumps» on your skin usually show that you are what? | Very tired | Very hungry | Happy and warm | *Cold or scared
test: In autumn, geese fly in what shape? | straight lines | circles | squares | *V-shapes
test: What is a male goose called? | goose | *gander | gull | gosling
exam: «You goose!» said Sam, laughing, when I tripped over my shoelace. What does goose mean here? | *Silly | A big bird with webbed feet | A baby bird | Very hungry
